            },
            {
                "date": "2024-03-08",
                "text": "In the rare case where the legal targets no longer all have equal toughness (probably because of a triggered ability or special action) when V.A.T.S. tries to resolve, it won’t resolve. None of the chosen creatures will be destroyed."
            },
            {
                "date": "2024-03-08",
                "text": "Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack."
            },
            {
                "date": "2024-03-08",
                "text": "Split second doesn’t stop triggered abilities from triggering. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal."
            }
        ]
    }
}

